    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the ratio of the volumes of two cubes, we first need to determine the volumes of each cube.\n\nThe formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a cube with edge length \\( s \\) is:\n\\[\nV = s^3\n\\]\n\nFirst, we calculate the volume of the cube with an edge length of 6 inches. The edge length is given as 6 inches, so we have:\n\\[\nV_1 = 6^3 = 6 \\times 6 \\times 6 = 216 \\text{ cubic inches}\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the volume of the cube with an edge length of 1 foot. Since 1 foot is equal to 12 inches (1 foot = 12 inches), the edge length of this cube is 12 inches. Therefore, the volume is:\n\\[\nV_2 = 12^3 = 12 \\times 12 \\times 12 = 144 \\text{ cubic inches}\n\\]\n\nNow, we find the ratio of the volume of the first cube to the volume of the second cube:\n\\[\n\\text{Ratio} = \\frac{V_1}{V_2} = \\frac{216}{144}\n\\]\n\nTo simplify this fraction, we find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 216 and 144. The GCD of 216 and 144 is 72. We divide both the numerator and the denominator by their GCD:\n\\[\n\\frac{216 \\div 72}{144 \\div 72} = \\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nThus, the ratio of the volume of the cube with edge length six inches to the volume of the cube with edge length one foot is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{3}{2}}\n\\]",
